    "created_at": "2024-04-22T08:10:02Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-04-22T08:10:02Z",
    "body": "If we ever added https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/10164 then this mechanism wouldn't be enough to actually differentiate close watchers Vs others?\r\n\r\nHaving said that I think the idea of sending the events but uncancelable is probably fine for now. My only reservation is that it's likely lots of dialog cancel event handlers won't actually be checking the cancelable value and I wonder if that could lead to some issues? prevent default would be a no-op which is fine, but could they be running a side effect they only want to run if the dialog doesn't close?",
